ntdll: read BOOLEAN syscall arguments as the Windows ABI defines them.

A Windows-side caller guarantees only the low byte of a BOOLEAN argument. The x64 ABI
leaves the upper bits of any narrow integer argument undefined, and MSVC stores exactly
one byte for a BOOLEAN it passes on the stack, so the other seven bytes of that slot are
whatever the caller's stack held before. __wine_syscall_dispatcher copies the raw 64-bit
word into the SysV argument register and calls the C implementation with it.

That implementation is built with clang on macOS, and clang assumes -- as the SysV ABI
allows it to -- that narrow parameters arrive zero-extended to 32 bits, so it tests all
32 bits: NtQueryDirectoryObject compiles `restart ? 0 : *context` to `testl %r8d,%r8d`.
Garbage in bits 8-31 therefore reads as TRUE. Wine on Linux never sees this, because the
unix side there is built with GCC, whose callees read only the byte.

Measured on Diablo IV 3.1.0 (the 2026-06-30 patch), which inspects the process that
started it when that process is still alive -- the Battle.net Agent always is. The loader
opens its parent, reads its image path, and walks \DosDevices one entry at a time with
NtQueryDirectoryObject to map drive letters to devices. WINEDEBUG=+syscall shows what it
passed for the fifth argument, `restart`:

    this tree:    NtQueryDirectoryObject(00000168,0010cf00,00000400,00000001,6c006200610000,...)
    CrossOver:    NtQueryDirectoryObject(0000016c,0010cf00,00000400,00000001,00000000,...)

The low byte is 0 in both. Ours carries the UTF-16 text "abl" above it, left on the stack
by an earlier string operation; with it the walk restarted at entry 0 on every call,
1.13 million times in thirty seconds, and the game sat at 12 threads forever. Skipping the
check by starting the game with no parent, or killing the parent afterwards, does not
change this loop, which matches everything observed before the cause was known.

CrossOver 26.3 clears the same check against the same bottle only because its PE side is
built with GCC and binutils, which leaves zeros in that stack slot where clang/lld-built
code leaves a string. Its ntdll.so contains the identical `testl %r8d,%r8d`, so it carries
the same latent bug; disassembly of both is in the README.

Only NtQueryDirectoryObject is changed, because it is the one call measured. The helper is
in unix_private.h so that the other syscalls with stack-passed BOOLEAN arguments --
NtQueryDirectoryFile, NtQueryEaFile, NtSetTimer, NtLockFile, NtNotifyChangeDirectoryFile,
NtNotifyChangeKey, NtCreateEvent among them -- can be given the same one-line treatment
once a caller is seen to need it.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
@@ -425,6 +425,19 @@
     while (len--) *dst++ = (unsigned char)*src++;
 }
 
+/* Read a BOOLEAN syscall argument the way the Windows ABI defines it: only the low byte is
+ * meaningful. Windows-side callers guarantee nothing about the upper bits of a narrow
+ * argument, and MSVC stores exactly one byte for a stack-passed BOOLEAN, so the rest of the
+ * slot is whatever the stack held before. The syscall dispatcher hands that raw 64-bit word
+ * to this side unchanged, where clang assumes that narrow parameters arrive zero-extended to
+ * 32 bits -- a SysV convention Windows code does not follow -- and tests all 32 of them. The
+ * asm barrier makes the compiler drop that assumption and read the byte only. */
+static inline BOOLEAN boolean_arg( BOOLEAN value )
+{
+    __asm__( "" : "+r" (value) );
+    return value;
+}
+
 static inline void *get_signal_stack(void)
 {
     return (void *)(((ULONG_PTR)NtCurrentTeb() & ~signal_stack_mask) + teb_size);
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -2081,9 +2081,16 @@
                                         ULONG *context, ULONG *ret_size )
 {
     unsigned int status, i, count, total_len, pos, used_size, used_count, strpool_head;
-    ULONG index = restart ? 0 : *context;
     struct directory_entry *entries;
+    ULONG index;
 
+    /* Diablo IV's loader walks \DosDevices with this call, single entry at a time, and
+     * passes restart=FALSE in a stack slot whose upper bytes still hold an old string. Read
+     * only the byte, or the walk restarts at entry 0 on every call and never ends. */
+    single_entry = boolean_arg( single_entry );
+    restart = boolean_arg( restart );
+    index = restart ? 0 : *context;
+
     if (!(entries = malloc( size ))) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
 
     SERVER_START_REQ( get_directory_entries )
